# The open-mercato skill collection is vendored: `.claude/skills/om-*` and skills-lock.json are
# both committed. The committed tree is what makes a run reproducible; the lockfile's per-skill
# `computedHash` is provenance for each skill's SKILL.md entry point, not for its references/.
# (.ai/cezar/config.json does not pin a SHA - it never did, whatever this comment used to say.)
# `pnpm install-skills` refreshes both, and they move in the same commit (docs/agents/cezar.md).
#
# That script passes `--copy` because the `skills` CLI symlinks by default: without it the
# vendored directories are replaced by links into an untracked `.agents/skills/`, which reads as
# hundreds of deleted files and puts the collection outside review.
# `.agents/` is deliberately not ignored here - if it ever appears, the install was wrong.

# Per-run artefacts of the om pipeline. The launchers .ai/scripts/test-env-*.sh stay tracked
# so a fresh Cezar worktree can boot the QA environment.
.ai/qa/test-env.json
.ai/qa/test-env.env
.ai/qa/test-env.lock/
.ai/qa/test-env-boot.log
.ai/qa/test-env-build-cache.json
.ai/qa/artifacts_*/
# om-qa-buddy's knowledge base (module history, risk hotspots) stays on the host that ran it.
.ai/qa/knowledge-base/
.ai/tmp/
.impeccable/hook.cache.json

# super-board: per-machine state, answers, backups and recovery files
.claude/super-board/active
.claude/super-board/onboard-answers.json
.claude/super-board/onboard-staged/
.claude/super-board/backup/
.claude/super-board/inflight/
.claude/super-board/migrations/
.claude/super-board/upgrade.json
.claude/settings.json.bak-*
